[{"text":"FCClearScalarProducts[] SPD[p] = 0;","anchor":"cb12","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FCLoopTensorReduce[amp3, {topo3}]","anchor":"cb13","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\text{\\$Aborted}\\]","anchor":"cb13-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Using FCLoopFindTensorBasis we can construct an alternative basis and supply it to the reduction procedure. In this case we need to introduce an auxiliary vector n. For simplicity, we choose it to be light-like","anchor":"cb13-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FCLoopFindTensorBasis[{p}, {}, n]","anchor":"cb14","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\{\\{p,n\\},\\{\\},\\{\\}\\}\\]","anchor":"cb14-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"In this case to complete the reduction we need to use IBPs. Furthermore, the existing topology should be augmented to include the new auxiliary vector.","anchor":"cb14-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"amp3red = FCLoopTensorReduce[amp3, {topo3}, TensorReductionBasisChange -> {{p} -> {p, n}}, AuxiliaryMomenta -> {n}, FinalSubstitutions -> {SPD[n] -> 0}]","anchor":"cb15","section":"Examples"},{"text":"{newtopo, gliRule} = FCLoopAugmentTopology[topo3, {SFAD[{{0, q1 . n}}], SFAD[{{0, q2 . n}}]}]","anchor":"cb16","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\left\\{\\text{FCTopology}\\left(\\text{prop2LA},\\left\\{\\frac{1}{(\\text{q1}^2-m^2+i \\eta )},\\frac{1}{(\\text{q2}^2-m^2+i \\eta )},\\frac{1}{((\\text{q1}-\\text{q2})^2+i \\eta )},\\frac{1}{((\\text{q1}-p)^2+i \\eta )},\\frac{1}{((\\text{q2}-p)^2+i \\eta )},\\frac{1}{(n\\cdot \\;\\text{q1}+i \\eta )},\\frac{1}{(n\\cdot \\;\\text{q2}+i \\eta )}\\right\\},\\{\\text{q1},\\text{q2}\\},\\{p,n\\},\\{\\},\\{\\}\\right),\\text{FCGV}(\\text{AddPropagators})(\\{n\\}) G^{\\text{prop2L}}(\\text{n1$\\_$},\\text{n2$\\_$},\\text{n3$\\_$},\\text{n4$\\_$},\\text{n5$\\_$}):\\to G^{\\text{prop2LA}}(\\text{n1},\\text{n2},\\text{n3},\\text{n4},\\text{n5},0,0)\\right\\}","anchor":"cb16-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"In this form the expression can be converted into GLIs and passed to an IBP reduction tool","anchor":"cb16-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"amp3red /. gliRule","anchor":"cb17","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Not all cases of zero Gram determinants require an auxiliary vector. If the new basis can be constructed from a subset of the present external momenta, this should be sufficient for the reduction. Consider e.g. this threshold kinematics","anchor":"cb17-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FCClearScalarProducts[] SPD[p1] = mm; SPD[p2] = mm; SPD[p1, p2] = mm;","anchor":"cb18","section":"Examples"},{"text":"topo4 = FCTopology[\"tri1l\", {SFAD[{q, m^2}], SFAD[{q - p1, 0}], SFAD[{q - p2, 0}]}, {q}, {p1, p2}, {}, {}]","anchor":"cb19","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\text{FCTopology}\\left(\\text{tri1l},\\left\\{\\frac{1}{(q^2-m^2+i \\eta )},\\frac{1}{((q-\\text{p1})^2+i \\eta )},\\frac{1}{((q-\\text{p2})^2+i \\eta )}\\right\\},\\{q\\},\\{\\text{p1},\\text{p2}\\},\\{\\},\\{\\}\\right)","anchor":"cb19-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"amp4 = FCGV[\"GLIProduct\"][GSD[q] . GAD[\\[Mu]] . GSD[r], GLI[\"tri1l\", {1, 1, 1}]]","anchor":"cb20","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\text{FCGV}(\\text{GLIProduct})\\left((\\gamma \\cdot q).\\gamma ^{\\mu }.(\\gamma \\cdot r),G^{\\text{tri1l}}(1,1,1)\\right)","anchor":"cb20-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FCLoopTensorReduce[amp4, {topo4}]","anchor":"cb21","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\text{\\$Aborted}\\]","anchor":"cb21-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FCLoopFindTensorBasis[{p1, p2}, {}, n]","anchor":"cb22","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\left( \\begin{array}{c} \\;\\text{p1} \\\\ \\;\\text{p2} \\\\ \\;\\text{p2}\\to \\;\\text{p1} \\;\\text{FCGV}(\\text{Prefactor})(1) \\\\ \\end{array} \\right)\\]","anchor":"cb22-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Here the momenta p1 and p2 are obviously identical, so we need to do the reduction w.r.t p1 only","anchor":"cb22-1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FCLoopTensorReduce[amp4, {topo4}, TensorReductionBasisChange -> {{p1, p2} -> {p1}}]","anchor":"cb23","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\text{FCGV}(\\text{GLIProduct})\\left(\\frac{(\\text{p1}\\cdot q) (\\gamma \\cdot \\;\\text{p1}).\\gamma ^{\\mu }.(\\gamma \\cdot r)}{\\text{mm}},G^{\\text{tri1l}}(1,1,1)\\right)","anchor":"cb23-1","section":"Examples"}]